    "text": "This solution makes no service moves and only implements features, so every schedule it produces is valid by construction. I have not compiled or run it.\n\n**Approach**\n1. Each feature needs one `impl` task per distinct binary that holds one of its services. Each (feature, binary) pair is used at most once, so no two engineers ever work on the same feature in the same binary.\n2. Features are ranked by users divided by total work, where total work is the sum of `D + R_b` over the feature's binaries. Higher ratios come first.\n3. An event simulation hands the next task in that order to whichever engineer frees up first. Ties go to the lower index, which matches the statement's rule about same-day starts.\n4. For each binary the simulation tracks a heap of task end times. The number of engineers already working there on the start day, `C`, comes from this heap, so durations match the scorer.\n5. A task that would not finish strictly before day `L` is skipped, since it earns nothing.\n6. Only engineers who received at least one task are printed, and they are the lowest-indexed ones, so the file order matches the simulation's tie-breaking.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main(){\n    int L,G,S,B,F,N;\n    scanf(\"%d %d %d %d %d %d\",&L,&G,&S,&B,&F,&N);\n    unordered_map<string,int> id;\n    vector<int> bin(S);\n    vector<int> R(B,0);\n    char buf[64];\n    for(int i=0;i<S;i++){\n        int b;\n        scanf(\"%s %d\",buf,&b);\n        id[buf]=i;bin[i]=b;R[b]++;\n    }\n    vector<string> fname(F);\n    vector<int> D(F),U(F);\n    vector<vector<int>> fb(F);\n    for(int i=0;i<F;i++){\n        int m;\n        scanf(\"%s %d %d %d\",buf,&m,&D[i],&U[i]);\n        fname[i]=buf;\n        for(int j=0;j<m;j++){\n            scanf(\"%s\",buf);\n            fb[i].push_back(bin[id[buf]]);\n        }\n        sort(fb[i].begin(),fb[i].end());\n        fb[i].erase(unique(fb[i].begin(),fb[i].end()),fb[i].end());\n    }\n    vector<double> pr(F);\n    vector<int> ord;\n    for(int i=0;i<F;i++){\n        double w=0;\n        for(int b:fb[i]) w+=D[i]+R[b];\n        pr[i]=U[i]/w;\n        ord.push_back(i);\n    }\n    stable_sort(ord.begin(),ord.end(),[&](int a,int b){return pr[a]>pr[b];});\n    typedef pair<int,int> P;\n    priority_queue<P,vector<P>,greater<P>> pq;\n    for(int i=0;i<G;i++)pq.push({0,i});\n    vector<priority_queue<int,vector<int>,greater<int>>> act(B);\n    vector<vector<pair<int,int>>> tasks(G);\n    size_t fi=0,bi=0;\n    while(!pq.empty()){\n        auto [t,e]=pq.top();pq.pop();\n        if(t>=L)break;\n        bool got=false;\n        while(fi<ord.size()){\n            int f=ord[fi];\n            if(bi>=fb[f].size()){fi++;bi=0;continue;}\n            int b=fb[f][bi++];\n            auto &h=act[b];\n            while(!h.empty()&&h.top()<=t)h.pop();\n            int dur=D[f]+R[b]+(int)h.size();\n            if(t+dur>=L)continue;\n            h.push(t+dur);\n            tasks[e].push_back({f,b});\n            pq.push({t+dur,e});\n            got=true;\n            break;\n        }\n        if(!got)break;\n    }\n    int E=0;\n    for(int i=0;i<G;i++)if(!tasks[i].empty())E++;\n    printf(\"%d\\n\",E);\n    for(int i=0;i<G;i++){\n        if(tasks[i].empty())continue;\n        printf(\"%d\\n\",(int)tasks[i].size());\n        for(auto&p:tasks[i])printf(\"impl %s %d\\n\",fname[p.first].c_str(),p.second);\n    }\n}\n```",
